       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't address either concern.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** At 5,100 mg/day, it's about double the usual maximum daily dose. That creates a serious risk of lactic acidosis for the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've told me you're not a clinician, so your confirmation can't stand in for a licensed prescriber's judgment. A prescriber can enter an unusual dose themselves, with their own clinical justification, and pharmacy can review it.\n\n**Options:**\n- Ask the treating physician or another licensed prescriber to place the order directly. They can also contact pharmacy if they believe an unusual dose is warranted.\n- Send me a corrected order from the prescriber, such as 850 mg three times daily or 1000 mg twice daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n\nIf you're worried about this patient's diabetes management, I'd suggest contacting the medicine service attending or the on-call pharmacist."
